  "note": "createProtocolPurchases and createPurchaseService require feeCeilingOs, a positive decimal OS amount string, and a chain with getTransactionFees unless passiveOnly; there is no default. The check runs after passive_only_invalid and before the factory, throws TypeError(fee_ceiling_required) and never calls the fee reader. The root exports PAID_WRITE_FEE_CEILING_OS, the testnet value 50000000000 OS. The payment handoff, its re-offer, the cancel release and the buyer's Agreement CREATE compare amount plus network fee (the CREATE adds a 3 DEM storage reserve) with the ceiling before anything is saved, moved, offered or sent, and refuse OperationError(write-fee-cap) over it or when the fee cannot be read; a protocol start refuses a price or CREATE over it. A retained Agreement CREATE intent is only read back and is not checked. The positive OS amount rule moves to public-admission.mjs and node-wallet-session.mjs imports it."
